# Run artifacts: extracted workdirs (full repo checkouts), trajectories,
# diffs, grades. Large and machine-local — evidence is exported to the
# dashboard's instances.json layer, never committed raw.
#
# Written as `runs/**` and not `runs/` because git does not descend into an
# excluded DIRECTORY at all — with `runs/` no `!` rule below could ever match.
runs/**

# ONE narrow exception (Sriram, 2026-07-28). The delegation folders are the
# only proof that the cc-driver × Antigravity-SDK-worker cable actually ran:
# each pair is the exact prompt the driver handed the worker and the usage
# sidecar the SDK handed back (model, sdk version, Vertex project/location,
# token counts). They were unfindable — ignored here, and absent from GCS
# because the publisher is keyed to console studies and harness runs were
# never registered as one. 134 files, 760 KB across 10 delegated runs (62
# hand-offs: 6 SWE-bench Pro runs, 4 SDLC/kudos-wall), so the size argument
# above does not apply to them. Count last recounted 2026-07-29, after the two
# post-ceiling clean re-runs of 28 Jul were bundled; it grows by ~12 files per
# delegated run, which is the intended behaviour — recount, do not re-scope.
#
# Scope is deliberately tight: ONLY the delegation subfolder of a built
# evidence bundle. Everything else in runs/ — the 880 MB checkouts, the
# trajectories, the graded diffs, the agent home directories — stays ignored.
# bundle-run.mjs is what puts files here, and it credential-scans every one
# and refuses to write the bundle at all on a hit.
#
# The ladder is explicit because each level only tells git "descend into this
# directory"; the last line is the only one that un-ignores actual FILES.
# Everything at those depths that is not named here — workdir/, out/, grade/,
# the diffs, the manifests — is still matched by `runs/**` and stays ignored.
!runs/*/
!runs/*/*/
!runs/*/*/*/
!runs/*/*/*/evidence-bundle/
!runs/*/*/*/evidence-bundle/delegation/
!runs/*/*/*/evidence-bundle/delegation/*

# Antigravity SDK worker venv (gemini_worker.py's interpreter). ~171M of
# machine-local pip packages built per the sdk-probe/README.md steps; it is
# a build artifact, never source. GEMINI_WORKER_PYTHON can point elsewhere,
# but the default in-tree location must never be staged.
sdk-probe/sdkprobe/

# pnpm's content-addressable package store for the SDLC kind's container.
# It lives HERE rather than inside a run's workdir on purpose: pnpm requires
# its store on the same filesystem as node_modules to hardlink, and when it
# is not, pnpm silently relocates the store INTO the project — which put
# 5,238 store files inside the graded tree on 2026-07-26. Shared across runs,
# so it also removes a per-run network fetch. Safe to delete at any time;
# the next run repopulates it.
.pkg-store/

# Python bytecode caches (e.g. sdk-probe/__pycache__ from the probe scripts).
__pycache__/
*.pyc
